    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0464" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.71/171: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-01-08T12:00:00+03:00">January 8,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 8—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. I have learned from a source which I regard as reliable that the railroad
                    between Lwow and Przemysl has been cleared and ordered <pb facs="0465" n="453"
                        xml:id="pg453"/> to be kept cleared for the next [few?] days. The same
                    informant advised me that whereas until recently Rumanian forces had been
                    withdrawn from Bessarabia they have now entered the southern half of that
                    district and are engaged in fortifying it—although the main Rumanian defense
                    line is still on the Prut and Danube Rivers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
